  (:id "t-rented-machines" :type :task :title "Approved by the owner 2026-11-13, in progress: rented machines as first-class fleet members, built in order: (1) the machine record gains provider, provider id, hourly price, purpose, rented-by and a return-by time, and one command lists rented boxes with their cost and overdue state; (2) nova-fleet rent and return verbs for Latitude and AWS: rent creates the box, checks its hardware against the ask (NIC model, cores) and deletes it on a mismatch, joins it and writes the record; return removes its runners, tailnet entry, record and the box; AWS temporary boxes stay off the tailnet with no seat or secrets; (3) an idle report of rented boxes with no load for N minutes (2026-11-13: four Latitude boxes rented with the wrong NIC, rented boxes billing idle after their drivers died, teardown programs living in a session scratch folder)" :state :todo)
  (:id "t-ci-red-nightly-view" :type :task :title "Gap, needs the owner's go-ahead: a red scheduled (nightly) run notifies nobody and nothing shows the fleet's red scheduled runs in one place, so moo's nightly failed every day 2026-11-10 to 2026-11-21 at one commit (d6a57e8c) unseen until an unrelated PR hit the same error" :state :todo
   :note "Evidence (gh run list --repo mas-bandwidth/moo --branch main --limit 15, 2026-11-21): nightly success 11-08 and 11-09, failure every day 11-10 to 11-21, all at d6a57e8c; fixed in mas-bandwidth/moo#76 (merged 2026-11-21). Measurement 2026-11-21 (gh run list --event schedule per repository, newest run of each scheduled workflow among the last 30 scheduled runs): red today, conclusion failure: moo nightly (11-21); nova-sprint nightly (11-21); hydrogen upstream drift (11-20); schema Squirrel all-port differential, python leg nightly (11-21); rocketnet nightly, Nightly CI, nightly-watch, nightly-toolchains, nightly big-endian system, Nightly framework integration, Fuzz (nightly), nightly-windows-sanitizers, Nightly Client Frame Time, Nightly Client Frame Budget, TLC records, nightly ubuntu lts vms, nightly-real-load (11-21). Cancelled today: schema Certify, CI full, Nightly conformance, schema-engine-is-the-oracle, schema-c-runs-hostile-corpus, schema-dart-runs-hostile-corpus, schema moo nightly fuzz, schema moo generated analyze strict gate, schema ruby nightly fuzz, Schema squirrel nightly fuzz, Squirrel runs the hostile corpus, Schema Lua version differential, ruby leg, Lobster fixed proof qualification. Every serialize.* port, serialize, apt, yojimbo, netcode, netcode.rs, nova-tools, reliable, reliable.rs and proton: green. Building anything here needs the owner's go-ahead.")
  (:id "t-ci-red-nightly-triage" :type :task :title "Unfinished, needs the owner's go-ahead: find the cause of every scheduled workflow that was red on 2026-11-21" :state :todo
   :note "The scan of 2026-11-21 (see ci-red-nightly-view) found red newest scheduled runs in rocketnet (13 workflows: nightly, Nightly CI, nightly-watch, nightly-toolchains, nightly big-endian system, Nightly framework integration, Fuzz (nightly), nightly-windows-sanitizers, Nightly Client Frame Time, Nightly Client Frame Budget, TLC records, nightly ubuntu lts vms, nightly-real-load), nova-sprint (nightly), hydrogen (upstream drift) and schema (Squirrel all-port differential, python leg nightly, plus 14 workflows whose newest run was cancelled: Certify, CI full, Nightly conformance, schema-engine-is-the-oracle, schema-c-runs-hostile-corpus, schema-dart-runs-hostile-corpus, schema moo nightly fuzz, schema moo generated analyze strict gate, schema ruby nightly fuzz, Schema squirrel nightly fuzz, Squirrel runs the hostile corpus, Schema Lua version differential, ruby leg, Lobster fixed proof qualification). A read-only triage was started the same day to find, for each, the first failing job and step, the date of the last green and first red run, and what changed between them (a commit, the hosted image move of 2026-11-10 to Ubuntu 26.04 and GCC 15.2, a runner offline or overloaded, the per-job time limit, a dependency, or a real test failure), grouped by cause. It was stopped the same day at the owner's word before it reached any conclusion: no cause is recorded, and none should be assumed. moo's nightly (same scan) was fixed by mas-bandwidth/moo#76; its first green run is expected on 2026-11-22, to be confirmed. Done means each red workflow has a named cause with its evidence and either a fix or its own roadmap entry in the repository it belongs to. Doing it needs the owner's go-ahead.")
  (:id "t-ci-hosted-image-drift" :type :task :title "Gap, needs the owner's go-ahead: nothing pins or records the image and compiler of GitHub-hosted jobs, so an ubuntu-latest move (24.04 to 26.04, GCC 15 rejecting a buffer under -Werror, moo#76) shows only as a red job; options, not chosen: pin the image version in workflows, or record the toolchain version per run and alert on a change" :state :todo
   :note "Evidence: moo nightly linux-gcc on 2026-11-09 logged Image: ubuntu-24.04 and passed; on 2026-11-21 it logged Image: ubuntu-26.04 and failed with moo_format.h:44:14: error: writing 16 bytes into a region of size 8 [-Werror=stringop-overflow=] (linux-gcc, compile-memcheck and compile-hashes red; macOS, Windows and linux-clang green). The GCC versions (13.3 before, 15.2 after) are as reported with the fix in mas-bandwidth/moo#76, not read from the logs. Building anything here needs the owner's go-ahead.")
  (:id "t-ci-cold-build-limit" :type :task :title "Gap, needs the owner's go-ahead: no check finds per-commit jobs whose cold build exceeds the runner hook's 120 s limit, which overrides a job's timeout-minutes, so each fails only when GitHub evicts its cache (serialize.moo 2026-11-21, cache unused 7 days, worked around by a daily run in serialize.moo#35)" :state :todo
   :note "Evidence: serialize.moo run 44909006657, job build the checked pinned moo on hetzner1-1, 13:28:16 to 13:30:24Z: Cache not found for input keys: moo-checked-Linux-X64-..., then CI rule: per-commit jobs finish in 2m at 13:30:21Z. The workflow sets timeout-minutes 5 for per-commit events; the hook's limit is enforced first. The limit: github_runner_ci_limit_seconds: 120 in cmd/nova-fleet/roles/github-runner/defaults/main.yml (one value for the fleet, never per repository), applied by roles/github-runner/tasks/ci-rules.yml into the hook directory's limit file, read by roles/github-runner/files/ci-rules/nova-ci-rules.sh (limit=120, then the limit file; limited exempts schedule and workflow_dispatch). Workaround: mas-bandwidth/serialize.moo#35, a daily scheduled run that keeps the cache in use. Building anything here needs the owner's go-ahead.")
  (:id "t-ci-limit-under-load" :type :task :title "Measurement for ci-cold-build-limit: under fleet load with bench work on the CI hosts, schema's lang-clean (elixir) was cancelled by the 120 s limit in 5 of 11 per-commit runs on 2026-11-21 (one after its last test printed OK); its green runs took 78-109 s" :state :todo
   :note "Evidence (schema CI fast jobs named lang-clean (elixir), 2026-11-21): cancelled on vision-2 13:26:36 to 13:28:41Z (log: OK at 13:28:38Z, then The operation was canceled), vision-6 13:44:37 to 13:46:45Z, hetzner2-7 13:59:27 to 14:01:36Z (log: CI rule: per-commit jobs finish in 2m at 14:01:32Z), vision-2 14:20:15 to 14:22:23Z, vision-5 14:27:30 to 14:28:52Z; green on amd-2-2, hetzner2-6, hetzner2-7, hetzner2-3 and vision-4 in 78 to 109 s. Bench work from several sessions ran on the same hosts as the runners. Building anything here needs the owner's go-ahead.")
  (:id "t-ci-runner-toolchain-env" :type :task :title "Question for the owner: a runner service's environment exports MOO and MOO_ANALYZE (~/sdk/moo-v1.3.0), which a repository's Makefile takes with ?= over the moo its job just built, so serialize.moo's ARM64 job tested the runner's moo on 2026-11-21; should runner-wide variables exist for tools repositories build themselves" :state :todo
   :note "Evidence: serialize.moo run 44909006657, job test on the pinned moo (ARM64) on the macOS runner studio-2. That runner's launchd plist holds MOO and MOO_ANALYZE naming ~/sdk/moo-v1.3.0/bin/moo and moo-analyze, beside every other SDK variable env.sh exports. serialize.moo's Makefile: MOO ?= $(MOO_DIST)/moo and MOO_ANALYZE ?= $(MOO_DIST)/moo-analyze. Where the values come from: cmd/nova-fleet/roles/sdk-toolchain/defaults/main.yml nova_sdk_env_files (MOO, MOO_ANALYZE, MOO_CHECKED), exported by roles/sdk-toolchain/templates/env.sh.j2; the service environment is the machine record's runner_env (github_runner_env in roles/github-runner/defaults/main.yml), written into the plist by roles/github-runner/templates/runner.plist.j2 and into the Linux unit by runner.service.j2. The two binaries were byte-identical that day, so the result stood, but the job did not test what it built. Deciding or building anything here needs the owner's go-ahead.")
  (:id "t-roadmap-cli-contract" :type :task :title "nova-roadmap meets the command-line contract" :state :todo
   :note "Today a refusal is two lines, nova-roadmap: REFUSED: <reason> then run: nova-roadmap help, and an unknown flag prints the flag package's text; TestCLIContract checks A3, A4 and A5 against one line naming the verb. The move into nova-tools kept every byte of output, so the change is its own step.")
  (:id "t-rented-return-by-enforced" :type :task :state :todo :title "A rented machine past its return_by is returned automatically or raises an alarm nobody has to look for (the owner, 2026-11-22)")))
